# flickos-layouts: flickos-layout reconfigure merges the tiling fragment into
# its labwc rc.xml overlay; 1.8: its panel button needs no process that
# stays (status once per change). flickos-settings: its rc.xml binds Super+T.
# fuzzel is only used by the panel's arrangement menu (right click).
Depends: python3,
         labwc,
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.8),
         flickos-settings (>= 1.11),
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: fuzzel
Description: opt-in window tiling for the FlickOS labwc session
 flick-tiler arranges windows side by side in the FlickOS labwc session:
 master and stack, columns, grid or one at a time, with gaps. New windows
 are tiled as they open; keybinds move the focus and the windows, and a
 panel button turns tiling on and off and chooses the arrangement.
 .
 labwc stays the window manager. flick-tiler places windows through
 labwc's own regions, which it rewrites as windows open and close, so
 turning it off gives the normal floating desktop back.
